Subject: [PATCH 2/2] aiter: add M=16384 prefill a16w16 GEMM rows for Llama-3.1-8B on gfx950

NOT SHIPPED -- effect is real but below what the rig can resolve, and it was only ever
measured stacked on top of patch 1/2, which regresses. See FINDINGS.md #5.

MEASUREMENT
  M=16384 is the prefill workhorse: 96 of 108 prefill batches in the fixed workload
  (ISL 8192, chunked-prefill-size 16384 -> 2 requests per batch). Every one of these
  shapes currently misses the tuned table and falls through to torch.

  Isolated, graph-captured (analysis/race_gemm_candidates.py --m 16384 --footprint-mb 0;
  no cache-busting needed, one gate_up call alone moves ~1.3 GB):
    o_proj   (4096, 4096)   torch  367.19 us -> hipblaslt:440237   353.81 us  +3.64%
    qkv_proj (6144, 4096)   torch  540.07 us -> hipblaslt:439059   531.07 us  +1.67%
    down_proj(4096,14336)   torch 1235.27 us -> hipblaslt:439112  1231.90 us  +0.27%
    gate_up  (28672,4096)   torch 2534.49 us -> nothing beat the fallback
  = 25.7 us of 4677 us of prefill GEMM per layer (0.55%), or 0.11% end-to-end.

  End-to-end (same 6 paired rounds as patch 1/2, both patches in one arm):
    mean TTFT 3986.2 ms -> 3978.6 ms (-0.19%), consistent with the isolated number.
    Throughput effect alone is ~0.03%, under the rig's 0.066% resolution at n=6.

  Note the tuner mis-ranked here too: its pick for down_proj (hipblaslt:439305, "+1.05%")
  re-times as a 0.09% LOSS in a graph, while 439112 -- which the tuner ranked 5th -- is the
  actual best. Every number above is the graph race, not the tuner.

APPLY
  cd /sgl-workspace/aiter && patch -p1 < <this file>
  rm -rf /tmp/aiter_configs      # merged table is regenerated only when absent
  # then restart the server: the GEMM table is consumed at HIP-graph capture time
  # revert: python3 analysis/deploy_gemm_rows.py revert   (restores from analysis/gemm_tune/base/)

BASE
  Applies on top of patch 0001, which creates this file.
